Keep BF16 rows BF16 when quantizing

Every arm opens with Tensor<FloatType>(from: tensor), which converts BF16
weights to F16. Z-Image and the Qwen family carry BF16 matmul rows inside
their _f16 checkpoints. The codecs store centroids and row scales in the
tensor's own dtype, and ccv_nnc_tensor_read cannot convert 16F to 16BF, so
the server crashes on its first generation with the quantized file. An
already-16-bit tensor is now passed through untouched, and only wider
tensors are narrowed.

A Z-Image Turbo quantized by this CLI differed from the macOS app's
quantization of the same source in exactly 238 rows, F16 here and BF16
there. The CLI's file crashed both gRPCServerCLI and the app.
